<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Sugar to soon seek 30,000T US soy/corn.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Sugar to soon seek 30,000T US soy/corn.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Taiwan Sugar Corp said on Thursday it would tender soon for 18,000 tonnes of No.2 or better U.S. yellow corn and 12,000 tonnes of No.2 or better U.S. yellow soybeans but gave no precise date.</p>
<p>Local traders said they expected the tender should take place within two weeks.</p>
<p>The maximum moisture limits for the combined shipment would be 14.5 percent for the corn and 13.5 percent for the soybeans.</p>
<p>Details for the tender as follow:</p>
<p>Shipment Tonne  Date/Location</p>
<p> Soybean  12,000 U.S. Gulf	Pacific N.W.</p>
<p> Corn     18,000 Dec 1-15	 Dec 15-31</p>
<p>--Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
